<step2>
<ptxt>Inspect Rear Power Window Regulator Switch Assembly (Rear LH)</ptxt>
<step3>
<ptxt>Disconnect the rear power window regulator switch assembly (rear LH) connector.</ptxt>
</step3>
<step3>
<ptxt>Using SST (Toyota electrical tester), measure the resistance between each terminal of the vehicle side wire harness connector of the rear power window regulator switch assembly (rear LH).</ptxt>
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09082-00030</s-number>
<s-number>09083-00170</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<spec>
<title>Resistance</title>
<table>
<tgroup cols="3">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="1.38in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="1.38in"/>
<colspec colname="COL3" colwidth="1.37in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Tester Connection (Terminal Symbol)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Condition</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Standard</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>1 (GND) ←→ Body ground</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Always</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Below 1 Ω</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
<atten4>
<ptxt>If the result is not as specified, there may be a malfunction on the vehicle side.</ptxt>
</atten4>
</step3>
<step3>
<ptxt>Connect the rear power window regulator switch assembly (rear LH) connector.</ptxt>
</step3>
<step3>
<ptxt>Measure the voltage between each terminal of the rear power window regulator switch assembly (rear LH) connector.</ptxt>
<spec>
<title>Voltage</title>
<table pgwide="1">
<tgroup cols="3">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="1.42in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="4.25in"/>
<colspec colname="COL3" colwidth="1.41in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Tester Connection (Terminal Symbol)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Condition</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Standard</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>6(UP) ←→ 1(GND)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>/IG ON</ptxt>
<ptxt>• Rear power window regulator switch assembly (rear LH) OFF → UP</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>11 to 14 V → 1 V or less</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>7(DOWN) ←→ 1(GND)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>/IG ON</ptxt>
<ptxt>• Rear power window regulator switch assembly (rear LH) OFF → DOWN</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>11 to 14 V → 1 V or less</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>8(AUTO) ←→ 1(GND)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>/IG ON</ptxt>
<ptxt>• Rear power window regulator switch assembly (rear LH) OFF → UP (auto operation) → Door glass fully closed</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>11 to 14 V → 1 V or less → 11 to 14 V</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>8(AUTO) ←→ 1(GND)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>/IG ON</ptxt>
<ptxt>• Rear power window regulator switch assembly (rear LH) OFF → DOWN (auto operation) → Door glass fully open</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>11 to 14 V → 1 V or less → 11 to 14 V</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>4(LED) ←→ 1(GND)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>IG ON → approximately 45 seconds after IG OFF</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>11 to 14 V → 1 V or less</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
<atten4>
<ptxt>If the result is not as specified, the rear power window regulator switch assembly (rear LH) may be defective.</ptxt>
</atten4>
</step3>
</step2>
